                <pb facs="0326" n="254" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg254"/>

                <head>No. 31.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lowell to Earl Granville.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-03-28"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 28, 1882</date>.
                        (Received March 28.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: Referring to my note of yesterday, I
                    have the honor to acquaint you that I have received this morning an additional
                    telegram from Mr. Frelinghuysen, requesting me to inform your lordship that the
                    British subject Lane, on whose behalf Mr. West intervened on the 24th instant,
                    asking for a speedy trial, is now being tried. It appears that all the delays
                    and continuances in this case have been made on the motion of Lane’s
                    counsel.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. R. LOWELL.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
